  BOTH DIALS ARE INERT, AND THAT IS THE FINDING, NOT A DEFECT OF THE GRID:
   (i) CLAIM SET collapses.  Requiring a RECOVERABLE comparison set (>= 2 named
       comparands) IS the C_STRICT predicate, so C_PROX and C_ALL admit 179 and 596
       extra ADJUDICATING units that name too few comparands to be scored at all.
       The scorable population is 79 at all three settings.  The record's widest-dial
       talk is therefore 0.8830 SET-UNSTATED: it adjudicates without writing
       down what it adjudicated against.
  (ii) TAU collapses.  GROSS's measured degenerate share is 0.9024 at tau = 0.02 and
       1.0000 at 0.05 / 0.10 / 0.20, and no other ladder crosses 0.50 at any tau, so
       exposure is a GROSS-membership test at every bar in the queue's range.  The
       bootstrap puts GROSS's ratio in [0.0005, 0.0254] at the 5th/95th percentile on
       all three panels — degenerate with room to spare, not a point read.

