ARM 4 — WHICH HEADLINE FORM THE EXPOSURE ACTUALLY BITES (1223's three readings)
============================================================================================================
  H_RUNNERUP  widest vs SECOND-widest        — a degenerate member is never top-2: IMMUNE
  H_NARROWEST widest vs NARROWEST in the set — the degenerate member IS the narrowest
  H_ANY       any ordered pair is decisive   — the degenerate member supplies a pair

  Measured on the priced ladders: for each (panel, fold) and each headline form, which
  ladder the form names, and whether that name CHANGES when the degenerate members are
  struck from the set at tau = 0.05.

    H_RUNNERUP   the named ladder MOVES at 0.0000 of 41 (panel, fold) cells when degenerate members are struck
    H_NARROWEST  the named ladder MOVES at 0.0000 of 41 (panel, fold) cells when degenerate members are struck
    H_ANY        the named ladder MOVES at 0.0000 of 41 (panel, fold) cells when degenerate members are struck
  [PASS] G4 H_RUNNERUP is immune to striking degenerate members (1223's prediction): 0.0000 (target == 0.0000)

  WHICH LADDER EACH FORM NAMES DOES NOT MOVE — but that is NOT what 1223's channel is.
  The degenerate member enters through the MARGIN the call is made on, i.e. the ratio
  widest/narrowest the bar is asked to adjudicate.  Measured directly:
    H_NARROWEST margin (widest/narrowest) WITH degenerate members: median    106.10  (min 27.62, max 4106.21)
    H_NARROWEST margin WITHOUT them (struck at tau = 0.05): median      4.03  (min 1.81, max 14.97)
    INFLATION FACTOR the degenerate member supplies: median x25.70
    So the record's set does not name a DIFFERENT ladder — it names the SAME one on a
    margin inflated by the factor above, which is exactly the channel 1223 priced.
