============================================================================================================
VERDICT
============================================================================================================
  ANSWER (C_STRICT, tau = 0.05): 74 of 79 committed
  widest-dial claims with a RECOVERABLE comparison set contained a degenerate member
  (0.9367).
  The exposure is a GROSS fact: GROSS's degenerate share at tau = 0.05 is 1.0000/1.0000/1.0000 on U56/B136/SMALL.
  But H_RUNNERUP moves at 0.0000 and H_ANY at 0.0000, so the exposure is a property of the HEADLINE FORM,
  not of the claim count.
  PRICE: striking degenerate members is worth +0.0000 of
  mean OOS Sharpe against the record's chooser and -0.0115 against doing nothing.
  KEEP paths: 4b (FULL halves AND rule-8 OOS, jointly) passes at 3 of 12 (chooser, panel) books,
  1 of which are TRADABLE at the protocol's 10 bps; 4a at 0 of 12 OOS books.
  Every tradable 4b pass here is the U56 ANCHOR book (N=20 equal weight, GROSS 0.75,
  weekly) which the record already carries as its 2026-09-04 candidate — no chooser
  studied here improves on it out of sample.
  VERDICT: KILL (capital) — the census answers the queue's question, but no chooser
  built from it clears 4b with a margin over doing nothing; this is a REPORTING
  finding, not a new tradable rule.

